^{:go/end 1500} (go/method PathValue "PathValue returns the value for the named path wildcard in the [ServeMux] pattern\nthat matched the request.\nIt returns the empty string if the request was not matched against a pattern\nor there is no such wildcard in the pattern.\n\nThe value is unescaped. For example, if the pattern \"/b/{bucket}\" matches\nthe path \"/b/a%2fb\", PathValue(\"bucket\") returns \"a/b\".\n" ^string [^{:tag (* Request)} r ^string name]
  (when [i (.patIndex r name)] (>= i 0)
    (return (aget (.-matches r) i)))

  (aget (.-otherValues r) name))





^{:go/end 1514} (go/method SetPathValue "SetPathValue sets name to value, so that subsequent calls to r.PathValue(name)\nreturn value.\nIt does not unescape value.\n" [^{:tag (* Request)} r ^string name ^string value]
